body=(f'<p class="sub"><a href="/directory/hosting.html">Hosting</a> › Hostinger</p><h1>Hostinger review for builders: plans, pricing, pros & cons</h1>'
 '<p class="sub">Checked 2026-10-16 on hostinger.com. Prices are the promotional 48-month rates shown in USD excluding VAT; they vary by region, currency and promotion. Always confirm on the official pricing page.</p>'
 '<p>Hostinger is a shared, cloud and VPS web host. Its web hosting page states it is trusted by 5M+ users, includes a free domain, email and SSL, offers a 30-day money-back guarantee and 24/7 support, and supports building with AI, WordPress, drag-and-drop or code (including Node.js on listed plans).</p>'
 +cta+'<h2>Web hosting plans (as listed on hostinger.com)</h2><div style="overflow-x:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Intro price</th><th>48-month term</th><th>Renews at</th><th>Highlights</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+rows+'</tbody></table></div>'
 '<p class="sub">Note the gap between intro and renewal pricing: the low monthly rate requires prepaying a long term, and renewal is roughly 3-4x higher.</p>'
 '<h2>Pros</h2><ul><li>Very low entry price on long terms.</li><li>Free domain for the first year, SSL and email included.</li><li>30-day money-back guarantee.</li><li>WordPress plus Node.js support on listed plans; AI website builder credits included.</li></ul>'
 '<h2>Cons</h2><ul><li>Headline price needs a 48-month prepay; renewals are much higher.</li><li>Free domain and mailboxes are for the first year only.</li><li>Shared hosting is not built for heavy serverless/edge apps: for Next.js or AI apps with server functions, platforms like <a href="/tools/vercel.html">Vercel</a>, <a href="/tools/netlify.html">Netlify</a> or <a href="/tools/render.html">Render</a> are usually a better fit.</li></ul>'
 '<h2>Who it is for</h2><p>Bloggers, small businesses, WordPress sites, portfolios and simple stores that want an all-in-one host with domain and email on a tight budget. Less suited to teams deploying git-based full-stack apps who want preview deployments per branch.</p>'
 '<div class="card"><h2>Deals</h2><p>Verified code not available yet. The discounts above are Hostinger\'s own public pricing, not a code from us.</p></div>'
 +cta+'<p class="sub">Compare all <a href="/directory/hosting.html">hosting & deployment tools</a>. Affiliate disclosure: this link may become an affiliate link in future; it currently goes to the official site.</p>')
